# Code owners for this Autoform project.
#
# Two Autoform control paths decide what CI accepts, and a pull request can
# change them along with the work under review:
#
#   /blueprint/roadmap/README.md  its open_statements setting decides whether
#                                 a theorem may merge with a sorry proof
#   /.github/                     the workflows, the audit script, and this file
#
# The Lean project's own build controls decide what CI compiles: its Lake
# configuration (lakefile.toml or lakefile.lean), lean-toolchain, and
# lake-manifest.json. Add rules for them too if their changes should wait
# for an owner.
#
# To use the rules, replace @OWNER with GitHub users, or visible teams, that
# have write access to the repository, and uncomment them. GitHub then asks
# those owners to review pull requests that change these paths. A merge waits
# for their approval only once a branch protection rule or an active ruleset
# for the default branch turns on "Require a pull request before merging",
# "Require review from Code Owners", and "Dismiss stale pull request
# approvals when new commits are pushed", and then only for those the rule
# does not exempt. A branch protection rule exempts repository administrators
# and custom roles with the "bypass branch protections" permission unless "Do
# not allow bypassing the above settings" is on, and exempts anyone listed
# under "Allow specified actors to bypass required pull requests"; a ruleset
# exempts everyone on its bypass list. An administrator, or a custom role
# with the "edit repository rules" permission, can also change or remove the
# rule.
#
# GitHub reads only the first of .github/CODEOWNERS, CODEOWNERS and
# docs/CODEOWNERS that exists. A project that keeps its rules in one of the
# others should add these two lines there and delete this file.

# /blueprint/roadmap/README.md @OWNER
# /.github/ @OWNER
